This is not an uncommon problem.  After your ascension run being
freakishly well-kitted-out with +5GDSM, +5 speed boots and intrinsic
speed, everything identified, and your pick of artifact weapons, it is
really easy to think you're war incarnate and forget that at the early
levels, you are totally newt-bait.

My first ascension was also a Valkyrie... I read yours when you posted
and it was very similar.  I started back with random characters after
that, and died a lot.  But then I decided to get back to my paranoid,
everything-is-out-to-get-me, E-ing a lot early character mindset, and
about a week later I got my second ascension with a (genoless) Gnomish
Ranger. Ranger playstyle is somewhat different from a Valk but I
thought it was pretty fun.

Both of my ascensions so far have had pretty phenomenal luck ... my
first Valk got some lucky polypets and found a minetown magic lamp and
a nice bones file.  My Ranger found a /WoW 0:2 in a shop on dlvl9.  My
current Samurai (who of course has not ascended yet) lucked out with
early dragon scales and a couple of good bones files.  Of course, they
all had to survive some pretty lousy luck first, either from a
polytrap, near-starvation, or just getting beat half to death, before
they got so "lucky."

So, for "moral support" relax, the post-first-ascension slump is not
unusual and things will get better.  And for "suggestions" I don't have
a specific character class to suggest, but playstyle-wise, just keep in
mind you aren't war incarnate anymore, and a soldier ant definitely can
catch you and will kill you if he does.  And you're not MR anymore
(unless you're a Wizard, which is a pretty far-different playstyle from
Valk I've heard) so a polytrap can definitely ruin your day.



